The 1927–28 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 40th season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1920/celtic1928.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1927-28|website=Londonhearts.com|accessdate=2 April 2019}}</ref> and the [[Scottish Cup]].

After having won either the league or the cup in the previous three campaigns, Celtic ended the season runner-up in both competitions. In the league they ended five points below champions [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]], to whom they also lost the Scottish Cup final, 4-0.

